WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:02.060
This is the last and final season.

2
00:00:02.060 --> 00:00:03.700
What, how is everyone gonna cope

3
00:00:03.700 --> 00:00:08.217
without a show that is so representative of life?

4
00:00:08.217 --> 00:00:10.350
"This Is Us" is about everyone.

5
00:00:10.350 --> 00:00:13.220
Brilliant title too, because it brings everyone in.

6
00:00:13.220 --> 00:00:14.450
It is a great title.

7
00:00:14.450 --> 00:00:17.050
It's better than the untitled Dan Fogelman project

8
00:00:17.050 --> 00:00:19.294
which it was when I auditioned for it.

9
00:00:19.294 --> 00:00:20.700
(Drew laughing)

10
00:00:20.700 --> 00:00:22.140
So "This Is Us",

11
00:00:22.140 --> 00:00:24.260 line:15%
what he landed on was that

12
00:00:24.260 --> 00:00:27.790 line:15%
our creator, Dan Fogelman really wanted to create a show

13
00:00:27.790 --> 00:00:29.850 line:15%
where everybody could see themselves.

14
00:00:29.850 --> 00:00:32.460
And I remember people asking me

15
00:00:32.460 --> 00:00:34.220
when did you know you had a hit?

16
00:00:34.220 --> 00:00:37.510
And, but I remember around episode four or so

17
00:00:37.510 --> 00:00:39.400
which was "The Swimming Pool".

18
00:00:39.400 --> 00:00:42.280
And I had a cousin of mine call me

19
00:00:42.280 --> 00:00:45.150
and she's a plus sized woman.

20
00:00:45.150 --> 00:00:47.270
She was adopted. Right?

21
00:00:47.270 --> 00:00:48.670
And she said, Sterling

22
00:00:48.670 --> 00:00:52.220
I know you're real excited about this OJ thing you just did.

23
00:00:52.220 --> 00:00:53.560
'Cause I had just done that.

24
00:00:53.560 --> 00:00:55.440
But she said, this "This Is Us",

25
00:00:55.440 --> 00:00:57.610
she says, this show is church.

26
00:00:57.610 --> 00:00:59.120
It is therapy.

27
00:00:59.120 --> 00:00:59.960
It is healing.

28
00:00:59.960 --> 00:01:03.840
She says, I see myself in Kate and Kevin and Randall.

29
00:01:03.840 --> 00:01:07.440
Like the way that this show affects my life,

30
00:01:07.440 --> 00:01:10.340
it's like you're saving me money on therapy

31
00:01:10.340 --> 00:01:13.290
by virtue of coming into my home every Tuesday

32
00:01:13.290 --> 00:01:15.790
and allowing me to process all this stuff

33
00:01:15.790 --> 00:01:18.120
that has happened in the past.

34
00:01:18.120 --> 00:01:20.510
I don't know what we'll do without it.

35
00:01:20.510 --> 00:01:23.843
I'm sure something else will come along that is lovely.

36
00:01:25.310 --> 00:01:26.420
I'm gonna miss it.

37
00:01:26.420 --> 00:01:30.407
We're gonna miss telling the story of the Pearson family.

38
00:01:30.407 --> 00:01:34.500
And I know I've talked to your producers about this whatnot.

39
00:01:34.500 --> 00:01:36.780
The good thing that I feel about the show

40
00:01:36.780 --> 00:01:39.770
is that Fogelman always wanted to do six seasons.

41
00:01:39.770 --> 00:01:42.090
So he had a beginning, middle and end

42
00:01:42.090 --> 00:01:44.580
that he wanted to like see this thing through with.

43
00:01:44.580 --> 00:01:46.610
And so we're not gonna have anything that like

44
00:01:46.610 --> 00:01:51.520
goes on in perpetuity and hopefully we'll finish stronger.

45
00:01:51.520 --> 00:01:53.850
I hesitate to say this 'cause I love the show

46
00:01:53.850 --> 00:01:56.710
but we will finish stronger than "Game Of Thrones".

47
00:01:56.710 --> 00:01:57.952
All right.

48
00:01:57.952 --> 00:02:00.240
So I came across the article where you talked about

49
00:02:00.240 --> 00:02:02.990
sticking the landing and how you went to Dan Fogelman

50
00:02:02.990 --> 00:02:07.360
and said, we have to stick this landing.

51
00:02:07.360 --> 00:02:10.080
How are you feeling about it right now?

52
00:02:10.080 --> 00:02:10.994
I'm feeling really good.

53
00:02:10.994 --> 00:02:12.842
I feel like it's gonna be awesome.

54
00:02:12.842 --> 00:02:15.390
(audience clapping)

55
00:02:15.390 --> 00:02:20.280
I'm picturing like a 10 stick,

56
00:02:20.280 --> 00:02:25.170
like all the judges, a 10 and that perfect landing,

57
00:02:25.170 --> 00:02:27.350
because I'm so glad that you aspire that.

58
00:02:27.350 --> 00:02:28.960
It is important.

59
00:02:28.960 --> 00:02:31.240
And that you have your eye on the prize with that

60
00:02:31.240 --> 00:02:34.970
is so money and I'm just so excited to see it.

61
00:02:34.970 --> 00:02:36.140
Okay, when we come back,

62
00:02:36.140 --> 00:02:38.697
Sterling K Brown is going to bare it all.

63
00:02:38.697 --> 00:02:41.040
"This Is Us" secrets and more.

64
00:02:41.040 --> 00:02:42.632
Don't go anywhere.

65
00:02:42.632 --> 00:02:45.299 line:15%
(upbeat music)

